1
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:54,720
Come on, one car?

2
00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:01,310
Hey, buddy! Where's the fire?

3
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:03,190
Got kids living around here.

4
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:10,570
What?

5
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:26,960
Twenty minutes ago, an energy surge

6
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,540
knocked out power 
across the entire Pacific Northwest.

7
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:30,630
What do we know?

8
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:33,130
Well, our first instinct 
was it was an EMP.

9
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:36,630
But electromagnetic pulses 
don't have that kind of power.

10
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:39,300
NASA has ruled out 
meteor strikes or solar flares.

11
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,850
The Department of Energy says 
it's not a power plant malfunction.

12
00:03:41,890 --> 00:03:44,770
Well, sounds like we're really good 
at figuring out what it wasn't.

13
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:47,140
This could be a prelude 
to a larger attack.

14
00:03:47,230 --> 00:03:49,350
I'm suggesting we scramble 
the Fifth and Sixth Regiment.

15
00:03:49,390 --> 00:03:50,560
No, no, no, no.

16
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:53,190
This needs a much more sophisticated mind.

17
00:03:53,270 --> 00:03:55,070
Someone who understands technology.

18
00:03:55,150 --> 00:03:57,900
- You want to send in a lab rat? 
- Not just any lab rat.

19
00:03:57,990 --> 00:03:59,490
A lab rat with teeth.

20
00:03:59,570 --> 00:04:01,740
You're not suggesting 
who I think you're suggesting.

21
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,580
- I know, he's a little weird. 
- Weird?

22
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,200
- No. No way. 
- He's a psychological tire fire!

23
00:04:06,290 --> 00:04:09,710
But he's also brilliant. 
Five PhDs, IQ off the charts.

24
00:04:09,790 --> 00:04:12,460
And his drone tech is revolutionary!

25
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,420
You're sure he can handle this?

26
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:16,420
He has a perfect operations record.

27
00:04:16,510 --> 00:04:18,420
- Remember the coup in Pakistan? 
- No.

28
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:19,970
Or the uprising in Azerbaijanistan?

29
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:22,140
- That's not even a country. 
- Exactly.

30
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,430
And you can thank Robotnik for that.

31
00:04:24,510 --> 00:04:27,640
I can't believe you're 
bringing that freak into this.

32
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:30,060
Neither can I, but...

33
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,100
we have no choice.

34
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:58,920
What the...

35
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:22,530
Are you in charge here?

36
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,990
You've never seen 
anything like this before.

37
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:30,080
It says I'm the top banana 
in a world full of hungry little monkeys.

38
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,460
Allow me to clarify.

39
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:36,250
In a sequentially ranked hierarchy 
based on level of critical importance,

40
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:38,420
the disparity between us 
is too vast to quantify.

41
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:40,800
- Agent Stone? 
- The Doctor thinks you're basic.

42
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,970
I'm initiating a sweep sequence.

43
00:05:43,050 --> 00:05:45,640
Ten miles in every direction 
should suffice.

44
00:05:47,470 --> 00:05:49,430
Ah... my babies.

45
00:05:49,510 --> 00:05:52,520
Whoo! Look what came out of my egg sac.

46
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,690
You know what I love about machines?

47
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:58,980
They do what they're told. 
They follow their programming.

48
00:05:59,070 --> 00:06:02,400
They don't need time off to get drunk 
and put the boat in the water.

49
00:06:03,150 --> 00:06:04,990
Now you do what you're told.

50
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:07,780
Stand over there on the edge 
of your personal abyss...

51
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:10,870
and watch my machines do your job.

52
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:16,080
- Can you feel it, Stone? 
- I can feel it, Doctor.

53
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:19,380
It's evolution, Stone.

54
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:20,800
It's evolution!

55
00:06:56,830 --> 00:06:58,960
- Agent Stone? 
- Doctor.

56
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,960
Do you see anything useful in this image?

57
00:07:02,210 --> 00:07:04,970
- Nothing at all, Doctor. 
- Of course you don't.

58
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:06,970
Your eyes weren't 
expertly trained to spot tracks

59
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:09,590
by the Native American Shadow Wolves.

60
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,690
That's extraordinary.

61
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:25,570
No. What's extraordinary is, 
I've determined the exact height, weight

62
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:27,200
and spinal curvature of this creature,

63
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,780
and my computer 
can't find a single match for it

64
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:32,410
anywhere in Earth's animal kingdom.

65
00:07:33,490 --> 00:07:37,080
This blackout was not a terrorist attack, 
and that's no baby bigfoot.

66
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:41,590
This guy is something else...

67
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:44,630
entirely.

68
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:47,470
Divert all search units 
to the site of the footprint.

69
00:07:48,430 --> 00:07:50,930
That's one small step for man,

70
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:53,310
one giant leap for me.

71
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:06,780
Here we go.

72
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:08,400
It didn't work out on Earth, 
but that's okay.

73
00:08:08,450 --> 00:08:09,740
You're going to a safe world.

74
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:12,320
A nice, safe world full of mushrooms.

75
00:08:12,410 --> 00:08:15,580
Mushrooms that'll be your only friends.

76
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:17,580
That sounds awful. I can't do this.

77
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:19,710
You have to do it. 
There's no other option.

78
00:08:20,710 --> 00:08:22,790
All right.

79
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:26,760
SFPD, pending background check.

80
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,340
Paws in the air!

81
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:32,720
Uh, meow?

82
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:39,310
Ow!

83
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:44,270
"San... Francisco?"

84
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,920
No.

85
00:09:12,470 --> 00:09:14,010
What?

86
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:37,160
The blue devil.

87
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:53,470
- Donut Lord? 
- It can talk.

88
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:56,600
You're not... 
You're not here to abduct me, are you?

89
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,100
You abducted me.

90
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,850
Okay, that's a fair point. What are you?

91
00:10:01,930 --> 00:10:03,770
Why are you hiding out in my garage?

92
00:10:03,850 --> 00:10:05,190
I needed somewhere safe.

93
00:10:05,270 --> 00:10:07,650
And you're the only person 
I could think of, Donut Lord.

94
00:10:07,730 --> 00:10:09,070
Why do you keep calling me Donut Lord?

95
00:10:09,110 --> 00:10:11,990
'Cause you talk to donuts. 
And then eat them if they get out of line.

96
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:13,820
Again, fair.

97
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,320
Wait, wait, wait. 
Where are all the mushrooms?

98
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,910
Why am I still on Earth? What is...

99
00:10:16,990 --> 00:10:19,700
Oh, no! I lost my rings.

100
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:21,080
What?

101
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:29,380
What's happening? 
Is this your mother ship?

102
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:31,670
I'm not in the mood to get probed.

103
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:34,470
You think you're worried? 
I'm not even wearing pants.

104
00:10:38,010 --> 00:10:40,220
What the...

105
00:10:41,930 --> 00:10:43,390
- They're coming for me! 
- Who's coming for you?

106
00:10:43,430 --> 00:10:44,480
What's that got to do with me?

107
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,440
I don't have time to explain, 
but you have to help me.

108
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,560
No, I don't. Why?

109
00:10:48,650 --> 00:10:52,150
Well, my legs, which normally 
would be classified as lethal weapons,

110
00:10:52,230 --> 00:10:53,360
feel like spaghetti.

111
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:56,240
I need your help. Please. 
It's life or death.

112
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,750
Fine. Come with me.

113
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:22,180
All right, stay here. And be quiet.

114
00:11:26,230 --> 00:11:27,520
Hello there!

115
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,520
Can I help you?

116
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:34,780
Good morning, my rural chum.

117
00:11:36,190 --> 00:11:39,780
I'm... from the power company, 
investigating the blackout.

118
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:43,200
If you don't mind, I'd like to take 
a few readings inside your house?

119
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:44,950
No kidding? You're from the power company?

120
00:11:44,990 --> 00:11:46,580
- Mmm. 
- Oh, you must know my buddy Spencer.

121
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:49,370
- We play softball together. 
- Ah! Spence.

122
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,460
He's a good man.

123
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:55,000
- Yeah. Come on in! 
- Great.

124
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:56,460
Take all the readings you need.

125
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,300
Except, uh...

126
00:11:58,380 --> 00:12:01,430
doesn't the power company usually take 
their readings from outside the house?

127
00:12:01,510 --> 00:12:03,600
That way they can check them 
even if you're not home.

128
00:12:04,310 --> 00:12:06,640
Also, my buddy Spencer 
works for the gas company,

129
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:08,350
and he's more of an Ultimate Frisbee guy.

130
00:12:08,390 --> 00:12:11,020
So, you want to tell me 
why you think I'm dumb enough

131
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,650
to just let you walk inside my house?

132
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:23,830
- I'm sorry, Mister... 
- Wachowski.

133
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:25,790
But everyone calls me Tom.

134
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:27,750
Except my dentist, he calls me Tim.

135
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:30,790
But it's gone on for so long now 
that it would be weird if I corrected him.

136
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:33,670
Well, Tom, whose dentist calls him Tim,

137
00:12:33,750 --> 00:12:37,460
you may have noticed that this entire town 
has been experiencing a power outage.

138
00:12:37,550 --> 00:12:39,590
Yep, no lights. Picked up on that.

139
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:42,510
Twenty minutes ago, I tracked 
an energy pulse with a similar signature

140
00:12:42,590 --> 00:12:44,680
to the one that caused that disruption.

141
00:12:59,610 --> 00:13:01,530
Listen, uh, Mister...

142
00:13:01,610 --> 00:13:02,990
Doctor.

143
00:13:03,070 --> 00:13:05,740
Dr. Robotnik. But my dentist calls me Rob.

144
00:13:05,830 --> 00:13:07,540
Hmm.

145
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:10,080
Look, uh, Dr. Robotskeez.

146
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:13,170
Um, I'm sure what you're here for 
is very serious,

147
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:14,670
but it's got nothing to do with me.

148
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:16,000
You can ask anyone in town.

149
00:13:16,090 --> 00:13:18,050
- Everyone knows me. 
- I bet they do.

150
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:21,380
I'm sure you're hella popular 
with the Jebs and Merles and Billy Bobs,

151
00:13:21,470 --> 00:13:24,050
in this glorified gas-station rest stop.

152
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:26,260
Betcha go way back 
to the days of tippin' cows

153
00:13:26,350 --> 00:13:28,260
and playin' in a jug band!

154
00:13:31,230 --> 00:13:34,150
And maybe someday you'll achieve your goal

155
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:36,900
of getting a Costco card 
or adopting a Labradoodle.

156
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:42,570
But the reality is, I surpassed 
everything you're ever going to do...

157
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:45,450
before I was a toddler.

158
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:49,450
I was spitting out formulas 
while you were still spitting up formula.

159
00:13:49,950 --> 00:13:51,330
I was breastfed, actually.

160
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:54,420
Nice. Rub that in my orphan face.

161
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:56,330
Mr. Wachowski,

162
00:13:56,420 --> 00:14:01,130
are you familiar with US Code 904, 
Title 10, Article 104?

163
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,590
- Yeah, who isn't... 
- "Anyone...

164
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:07,430
who attempts to aid an enemy 
of the United States shall suffer death."

165
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:11,390
And if I'm the one that catches you,

166
00:14:11,470 --> 00:14:12,680
it'll be even worse.

167
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,100
Worse than death?

168
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:29,580
Compared to what I...

169
00:14:32,330 --> 00:14:33,960
- Old pipes. 
- Yeah.

170
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,500
Probably just the house settling.

171
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:37,250
Nothing to see here!

172
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:39,540
Hey!

173
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,300
Here's the thing.

174
00:14:47,890 --> 00:14:49,260
I'm never wrong.

175
00:14:50,010 --> 00:14:52,430
Well, first time for everything, I guess.

176
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:53,890
Would you like some cake?

177
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:57,270
I hear raccoons have the cleanest mouths 
of any animal that routinely eats garbage.

178
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:10,910
Look at that.

179
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:13,750
I was right.

180
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:16,080
Note the lack of surprise.

181
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:17,830
Shall we try this again?

182
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:32,220
I'm going to give you five seconds 
to tell me where it is.

183
00:15:32,310 --> 00:15:33,930
- Five... 
- I don't know what you're talking about.

184
00:15:33,970 --> 00:15:35,390
- Four. 
- Hey, tough guy. I'm a cop,

185
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,810
and you're threatening an officer.

186
00:15:36,850 --> 00:15:39,020
How can you threaten somebody 
who never existed?

187
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,520
Three...

188
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:42,440
Come on! Rack your brain.

189
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:47,240
You might be able to come up with some 
lame excuse to go on living, in two...

190
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,280
one.

191
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:51,490
Wait! Don't hurt him!

192
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:08,420
Stay behind me.

193
00:16:22,150 --> 00:16:23,440
Hiya!

194
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:37,870
Come on! We gotta get out of here.

195
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:59,310
Doctor! Are you okay?

196
00:16:59,850 --> 00:17:01,810
I saw a guy race out of here and thought...

197
00:17:01,890 --> 00:17:03,600
That you should stop them?

198
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:09,110
Whatever this creature is, 
it's our job to secure it,

199
00:17:09,190 --> 00:17:13,110
neutralize it, 
uncover the source of its power.

200
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,620
And if it resists...

201
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:18,910
we take it apart... piece by piece.

202
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:22,080
See what makes it tick.

203
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:24,790
- Stone? 
- Doctor?

204
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,500
Call Optical Illusions.

205
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:28,840
Tell them I need new frames.

206
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:31,010
They know what kind I like.

207
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:34,090
Oh, and bring that quill.

208
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:36,600
Yes, Doctor.

209
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,770
All right, there's 
gonna be rules on this trip.

210
00:17:42,810 --> 00:17:45,650
Number one, 
do exactly as I say all the time.

211
00:17:45,730 --> 00:17:47,820
- Got it? 
- Got it, Donut Lord.

212
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,530
Would you stop with the "Donut Lord"?

213
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:51,940
I have a name. It's Tom.

214
00:17:52,570 --> 00:17:53,570
I'm Sonic.

215
00:17:53,650 --> 00:17:55,990
Sonic. Sonic.

216
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:16,090
I'm gonna go check in with Wade, 
see if he knows what's going on.

217
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:17,220
Hello. Green Hills Police Department.

218
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:19,060
- Wade, it's me. 
<i>- Hi.</i>

219
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:20,430
I'm so glad that you called.

220
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:23,180
Uh, so, some guys came in 
asking some questions.

221
00:18:23,270 --> 00:18:25,270
Uh, they're a little creepy.

222
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:26,310
Wait, what kind of questions?

223
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:29,770
Um, questions about terrorism?

224
00:18:29,860 --> 00:18:32,990
I told them that 
I've gone ice fishing with Tom.

225
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:34,490
He doesn't know how to make a bomb.

226
00:18:34,570 --> 00:18:36,950
<i>He can't even make bait in the cold.</i>

227
00:18:37,030 --> 00:18:39,030
All right, Wade, listen to me. 
This is really important.

228
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:40,580
Don't tell them that we talked, okay?

229
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:46,210
You know, I think they already know.

230
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:50,670
Mr. Wachowski.

231
00:18:51,170 --> 00:18:52,210
Tom.

232
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:54,130
I want you to know 
that the only other person

233
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:57,430
who ever punched me in the face 
was the school bully.

234
00:18:57,510 --> 00:19:00,050
He hit me in the cafeteria, 
causing a blunt-force contusion

235
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:02,770
to the soft tissue 
surrounding my orbital bone.

236
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,890
Humiliated me in front of 
the entire school!

237
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,640
And do you know what I did in response?

238
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:09,860
Uh, I'm assuming that you reported him 
to the principal's office

239
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,860
'cause that kind of behavior 
is really unacceptable.

240
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:15,190
No. I examined the inefficiency of a world 
where brawn trumped brain,

241
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:18,240
and I used technology 
to resolve that inefficiency.

242
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:21,410
The boy ate his meals 
through a straw for a year.

243
00:19:21,490 --> 00:19:23,240
And I have never lost a fight again.

244
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:24,750
Until today.

245
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:26,500
Hey, hooray for me then, huh?

246
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:29,420
No, because you're about to become 
the bully with the straw!

247
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:32,090
I'm coming for you, Mr. Wachowski.

248
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:33,550
And when I catch you, I'll...

249
00:19:34,170 --> 00:19:36,090
Hello.

250
00:19:36,170 --> 00:19:37,260
Hello?

251
00:19:37,930 --> 00:19:38,930
Hello, hello, hello?

252
00:19:39,010 --> 00:19:42,260
I think he actually hung up, 
because I notice that the light isn't on.

253
00:19:42,350 --> 00:19:43,850
Thank you, Officer Brainfart.

254
00:19:43,930 --> 00:19:46,060
If you give me a second, 
I can get an outside line.

255
00:19:46,140 --> 00:19:48,350
No. Don't be bothered.

256
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:53,360
You just sit there and be "u"... 'seless.

257
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:26,850
<i>Thomas Wachowski, accused of committing 
an act of domestic terrorism.</i>

258
00:20:26,930 --> 00:20:29,770
<i>Wachowski is considered 
armed and dangerous.</i>

259
00:20:29,850 --> 00:20:31,730
<i>Any information regarding his whereabouts</i>

260
00:20:31,810 --> 00:20:34,570
<i>should be reported to 
local authorities immediately.</i>

261
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:42,280
Did he say where he was going?

262
00:20:45,910 --> 00:20:48,410
Maybe. Maybe not.

263
00:20:49,370 --> 00:20:50,670
Like I'd ever tell you.

264
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:53,920
Stand down, Agent Stone.

265
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,300
This well-meaning citizen 
obviously doesn't understand

266
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,670
the urgency of the matter.

267
00:21:00,590 --> 00:21:01,630
Really?

268
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:07,060
Now that's 
what I call good cop, bad cop.

269
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:10,230
Hoy!

270
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:12,020
Left yourself open.

271
00:21:14,610 --> 00:21:16,440
Judging by the quickest route 
to San Francisco,

272
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:19,650
the approximate speed of their vehicle, 
and local weather conditions...

273
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:22,700
they should be...

274
00:21:23,530 --> 00:21:25,320
right about...

275
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:27,910
here.

276
00:21:27,990 --> 00:21:30,450
- That's brilliant, sir. 
- Thanks...

277
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:32,460
for nothing.

278
00:21:45,890 --> 00:21:49,890
Eeny, meeny, miny...

279
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:51,890
mayhem.

280
00:22:06,450 --> 00:22:08,450
- Look, I get your poi... 
- Whoa!

281
00:22:09,830 --> 00:22:11,080
Yeah!

282
00:22:21,630 --> 00:22:23,760
Sonic!

283
00:22:24,380 --> 00:22:26,970
- Your body! 
- Oh, no, not again!

284
00:22:27,050 --> 00:22:28,100
Hey! Hold on!

285
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,930
- Why? 
- Because I'm gonna do this.

286
00:22:48,780 --> 00:22:50,080
Sonic!

287
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,450
Sonic!

288
00:22:59,040 --> 00:22:59,590
Is that all you got?

289
00:22:59,670 --> 00:23:01,590
No, but thank you for asking.

290
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:08,010
- Uh-oh. 
- Sonic! Get back in the truck!

291
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,720
Ha!

292
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:31,490
Incoming!

293
00:23:54,390 --> 00:23:56,430
Yes, we did it!

294
00:24:00,980 --> 00:24:03,610
We did not do it. Who <i>is</i> this guy?

295
00:24:03,690 --> 00:24:06,240
Ever wonder where 
your tax dollars are going?

296
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:07,360
My turn.

297
00:24:07,450 --> 00:24:09,950
Here, just keep us going straight. 
I put it in cruise control.

298
00:24:25,750 --> 00:24:27,840
Ha-ha! Whoo!

299
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:30,760
Oh!

300
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:34,140
Give me a big, fat break!

301
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:42,230
Aw, this one is cute. Let's keep him.

302
00:24:43,610 --> 00:24:44,610
Aah!

303
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:56,580
Buzz off.

304
00:24:56,660 --> 00:24:58,290
That doesn't sound good.

305
00:24:58,370 --> 00:25:00,710
- No, beeping is bad. Get rid of it! 
- I'm trying.

306
00:25:00,790 --> 00:25:02,540
Throw it out the win... Throw it anywhere!

307
00:25:02,630 --> 00:25:04,920
- I can't get it off. 
- All right, I'm pulling over.

308
00:25:12,930 --> 00:25:13,800
- Did I get it? 
- Nope.

309
00:25:15,970 --> 00:25:17,430
Here. Hold still.

310
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:20,600
It's going, it's going...

311
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:22,900
It's still here.

312
00:25:25,310 --> 00:25:26,360
Get off me.

313
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:37,080
Sonic!

314
00:25:44,500 --> 00:25:45,670
No, no, no, no, no.

315
00:25:52,590 --> 00:25:56,510
Hey. Come on. You're all right. 
Wake up. Wake up.

316
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:04,940
Did we get 'em?

317
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:07,650
Oh. No, there they are.

318
00:26:07,730 --> 00:26:10,230
They are real survivors, those two.

319
00:26:15,410 --> 00:26:16,740
Can we have a moment?

320
00:26:19,700 --> 00:26:21,120
Pin yourself to the wall.

321
00:26:22,540 --> 00:26:24,830
You know, I won't miss you 
when you're gone.

322
00:26:24,920 --> 00:26:28,790
Human beings are unreliable and stupid, 
and I care very little about them.

323
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:31,590
But my machines are diligent, relentless.

324
00:26:31,670 --> 00:26:33,510
They're everything to me!

325
00:26:35,470 --> 00:26:36,680
Huh?

326
00:26:56,740 --> 00:26:57,780
Mmm?

327
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:12,880
Come on, buddy.

328
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:15,340
You're gonna be all right. 
You'll be all right.

329
00:28:59,570 --> 00:29:02,570
I just thought you might like a latte 
with steamed Austrian goat milk.

330
00:29:03,490 --> 00:29:05,410
Who do I look like, an imbecile?

331
00:29:05,490 --> 00:29:08,700
Of course I want a latte. 
I love the way you make them!

332
00:29:15,540 --> 00:29:17,880
Ready the prototype.

333
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:19,720
With this kind of power,

334
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:23,720
my machines can finally reach 
their full potential.

335
00:29:30,230 --> 00:29:31,890
He's gonna be okay, Jojo.

336
00:29:33,190 --> 00:29:35,980
Oh, thank God. He's gonna be okay, right?

337
00:29:36,060 --> 00:29:38,570
I'm a vet, Tom. I don't even know 
what I'm looking at here.

338
00:29:38,650 --> 00:29:40,780
He's a hedgehog. Or so he says.

339
00:29:40,860 --> 00:29:42,530
- It talks? 
- Almost constantly.

340
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:45,240
Okay.

341
00:29:45,870 --> 00:29:47,160
- Holy... 
- What?

342
00:29:47,240 --> 00:29:48,700
His pulse is super-fast.

343
00:29:48,790 --> 00:29:50,620
That actually might be normal for him.

344
00:29:50,700 --> 00:29:52,330
I don't know. You gotta help him, Maddie.

345
00:29:52,410 --> 00:29:54,170
I don't know his physiology.

346
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:56,790
He doesn't seem to have any broken bones.

347
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:59,090
He's just really banged up.

348
00:30:00,630 --> 00:30:03,590
Oh, look at his poor little feet.

349
00:30:06,850 --> 00:30:09,430
Hang in there, buddy. 
You're gonna be all right.

350
00:30:10,810 --> 00:30:14,190
- So, this is it? 
- That's it. That's your pyramid.

351
00:30:14,270 --> 00:30:16,360
Wow, look at that thing!

352
00:30:16,440 --> 00:30:17,610
What happens now?

353
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:21,110
- Oh. He's... gone. 
- Yep.

354
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:24,820
No good. You need a special key 
to get to the roof.

355
00:30:25,860 --> 00:30:27,200
What now?

356
00:30:27,820 --> 00:30:30,620
Time for me to abuse 
the power entrusted to me.

357
00:30:40,840 --> 00:30:42,050
We got a jumper on the roof.

358
00:30:42,130 --> 00:30:45,010
Gotta get up there fast or we're gonna 
have a human pancake on our hands.

359
00:30:45,510 --> 00:30:47,300
You came all the way from Montana.

360
00:30:48,510 --> 00:30:50,140
Yeah. That's how serious it is.

361
00:30:55,020 --> 00:30:56,020
Okay.

362
00:30:57,900 --> 00:30:59,230
You just saved a life.

363
00:31:09,580 --> 00:31:10,830
All right. What are we looking for?

364
00:31:14,080 --> 00:31:15,500
This.

365
00:31:16,330 --> 00:31:18,290
Okay. What happens now?

366
00:31:18,380 --> 00:31:20,210
Now all I have to do 
is think of where I want

367
00:31:20,290 --> 00:31:22,420
the other end of the ring 
to appear, and I throw it.

368
00:31:22,500 --> 00:31:24,550
So that's it? We did it?

369
00:31:24,630 --> 00:31:25,970
Yeah. We did it!

370
00:31:26,300 --> 00:31:27,720
- All right.

371
00:31:28,930 --> 00:31:30,890
- Um, you gotta go, right? 
- Yeah, I gotta go.

372
00:31:30,930 --> 00:31:32,180
I gotta go. We gotta go too.

373
00:31:32,260 --> 00:31:33,850
See... All right, bye-bye.

374
00:32:17,230 --> 00:32:19,850
Welcome to San Francisco, Mr. Wachowski.

375
00:32:20,940 --> 00:32:22,730
Are you enjoying the clam chowder?

376
00:32:22,810 --> 00:32:25,030
It's the government wack job 
who keeps trying to kill us.

377
00:32:25,070 --> 00:32:26,530
Unsuccessfully!

378
00:32:26,610 --> 00:32:28,530
Nice of you to swing by 
on your way to Comic-Con.

379
00:32:28,570 --> 00:32:29,780
Yeah, what are you wearing?

380
00:32:31,950 --> 00:32:36,290
It's a flight suit, designed to modulate 
my body temperature and reduce drag.

381
00:32:36,370 --> 00:32:37,960
Yeah, and yet you still are one.

382
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:39,830
Ooh-hoo! Good one.

383
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:41,880
You are catching fire, Thomas.

384
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:44,340
Oh, and speaking of heat, 
I see you've taken a lover.

385
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:46,050
Does she have a name

386
00:32:46,130 --> 00:32:48,550
or should we just call her 
"collateral damage"?

387
00:32:48,630 --> 00:32:49,760
Hey, watch your mouth.

388
00:32:49,840 --> 00:32:51,340
Unless you want a little more 
of what I gave you earlier?

389
00:32:52,300 --> 00:32:53,640
I punched him in the face.

390
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:56,310
The time for talking is over! 
It's time to push buttons.

391
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:12,530
I was not expecting that.

392
00:33:12,610 --> 00:33:15,330
But I was expecting not to expect 
something, so it doesn't count.

393
00:33:58,080 --> 00:33:59,750
Pew, pew-pew-pew, pew-pew-pew-pew!

394
00:34:03,830 --> 00:34:06,670
Oh!

395
00:34:25,900 --> 00:34:28,320
Whoa, whoa, whoa! No, no, no!

396
00:34:37,570 --> 00:34:38,450
Aah.

397
00:34:39,740 --> 00:34:42,100
Can I give you one genius piece of advice?

398
00:34:43,460 --> 00:34:45,080
Don't run.

399
00:34:45,170 --> 00:34:47,500
It'll only hurt more if you do.

400
00:34:47,580 --> 00:34:49,880
And it's bad for your joints. 
They've proved it.

401
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:52,300
All right, Eggman. You wanna get fast?

402
00:34:52,380 --> 00:34:53,550
Let's get fast.

403
00:34:56,800 --> 00:34:58,180
The hard way it is.

404
00:35:17,410 --> 00:35:19,120
That was an illegal left, by the way.

405
00:35:38,840 --> 00:35:40,100
How is this possible?

406
00:35:40,180 --> 00:35:42,260
No one's ever caught up to me before.

407
00:35:50,060 --> 00:35:51,900
Coming through!

408
00:35:51,980 --> 00:35:52,980
<i>Sacrebleu!</i>

409
00:35:54,110 --> 00:35:56,280
<i>Excusez-moi, monsieur!</i>

410
00:36:00,240 --> 00:36:02,490
Here we go. Room to open it up.

411
00:36:11,750 --> 00:36:13,000
I can't lose him!

412
00:36:30,350 --> 00:36:32,400
Lost visual contact.

413
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:41,110
You're not allowed up there! 
It's one of the Seven Wonders!

414
00:37:05,430 --> 00:37:06,970
Get out of here!

415
00:37:14,900 --> 00:37:18,150
You're an astonishing little creature.

416
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:22,660
It'll be fun to take you back to the lab

417
00:37:22,740 --> 00:37:24,990
for a litany of invasive 
exploratory procedures.

418
00:37:25,950 --> 00:37:27,620
Any last words?

419
00:37:27,700 --> 00:37:31,330
Guac. I like that word.

420
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:35,380
I don't have to tell you how 
many scientific breakthroughs

421
00:37:35,420 --> 00:37:37,800
have been made possible by animal testing.

422
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:38,960
You're being very selfish.

423
00:37:39,050 --> 00:37:40,220
Going my way?

424
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:41,510
What the...

425
00:37:46,930 --> 00:37:48,890
Who the hell do you think you are?

426
00:37:52,230 --> 00:37:53,730
I'm the Donut Lord, you son of a...

427
00:37:58,860 --> 00:38:00,570
Autopilot, adjust.

428
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:02,740
Why?

429
00:38:02,820 --> 00:38:06,120
Why would you throw 
your life away for this thing?

430
00:38:06,200 --> 00:38:07,580
That's why I don't have friends.

431
00:38:07,660 --> 00:38:09,740
Next thing you know, 
you're somebody's best man.

432
00:38:09,830 --> 00:38:11,370
They want to have the wedding out of town.

433
00:38:11,410 --> 00:38:13,460
Like nobody has anything better to do!

434
00:38:14,290 --> 00:38:16,330
Anyway, where were we?

435
00:38:16,420 --> 00:38:18,960
Oh, yes. You were about to die.

436
00:38:21,210 --> 00:38:22,920
That's our sheriff you're messing with.

437
00:38:23,630 --> 00:38:25,550
I don't mean to be indelicate here,

438
00:38:25,640 --> 00:38:29,060
but someone should get some ice, 
keep the body fresh.

439
00:38:32,060 --> 00:38:34,310
He's just a silly little alien.

440
00:38:34,810 --> 00:38:36,230
He didn't belong here!

441
00:39:01,340 --> 00:39:02,510
Everyone, get back!

442
00:39:06,260 --> 00:39:08,930
I think you have something 
that belongs to me.

443
00:39:09,720 --> 00:39:10,720
Whoa.

444
00:40:16,750 --> 00:40:18,870
Ooh! Now you've done it!

445
00:41:17,810 --> 00:41:18,980
- I think these belong to you.

446
00:41:21,900 --> 00:41:24,980
- You did pretty good, space hog. 
- Thanks, Donut Lord.

447
00:41:25,360 --> 00:41:27,820
All right, everybody. Nothing to see here.

448
00:41:27,900 --> 00:41:28,990
Let's disperse.

449
00:41:29,070 --> 00:41:30,950
Just another ordinary day in Green Hills.

450
00:41:39,450 --> 00:41:42,960
My grasp on sanity remains... absolute.

451
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:46,250
Isn't that right, Agent Stone?

452
00:41:51,470 --> 00:41:53,590
Why don't you get a head start?

453
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:58,680
Do some rock-connaissance.

454
00:41:58,770 --> 00:42:01,680
Rock-connaissance! 
Come on! That's hilarious!

455
00:42:01,770 --> 00:42:03,520
What's the matter with you?

456
00:42:03,600 --> 00:42:06,810
Here's the "sitch." Uninhabited planet.

457
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:12,360
No resources, no supplies, 
no apparent way home.

458
00:42:14,910 --> 00:42:16,490
A lesser man would die here.

459
00:42:19,790 --> 00:42:21,450
I'll be home by Christmas.

460
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:43,020
Rock-connaissance!

461
00:42:46,190 --> 00:42:48,110
Come on! Cheer up!

462
00:44:50,100 --> 00:44:52,560
If these readings are accurate, he's here.

463
00:44:52,650 --> 00:44:53,940
I found him.

464
00:44:54,020 --> 00:44:55,820
I just hope I'm not too late.
